{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.Common","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.Common","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.InnerProductSpace.EuclideanDist","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.InnerProductSpace.Dual","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Factorial.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.absMarkovTrace_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.absMarkovTrace_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":217,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/Common.lean#L217-L218","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.absMarkovTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.absMarkovTrace","kind":"def","line":211,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/Common.lean#L211-L215","doc":"**Absolute Markov trace** — the modulus of the Markov trace\nused in the QOU mass formula `M = ρ · m_e · |tr_M(T_w)|`.\nAlways non-negative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.markovTrace_linear","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.markovTrace_linear","kind":"theorem","line":198,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/Common.lean#L198-L209","doc":"The Markov trace is linear in its argument: this is the only structural\nproperty of `markovTrace` used by the SDP-uniqueness arguments downstream.\n\n**Was an `axiom` until 2026-08-26.** The stated ground was that the categorical\ndefinition had not been ported; that conflated the trace's *value* (genuinely\nnot formalised, and still carried opaquely in `markovTraceWeight`) with its\n*linearity*, which is a property of the shape `⟪w, ·⟫` and needs no value.\n`isLinearMap_iff_exists_weight` proves the two presentations are the same\nclass of functionals, so this costs nothing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.isLinearMap_iff_exists_weight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.isLinearMap_iff_exists_weight","kind":"theorem","line":177,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/Common.lean#L177-L196","doc":"**The two presentations have the same content.**\n\nA function `HeckeElement n → ℝ` is `ℝ`-linear **iff** it is `⟪w, ·⟫` for some\n`w`, and by `weight_unique` that `w` is unique. So \"an opaque function asserted\nto be linear\" and \"an opaque weight vector\" range over exactly the same\nfunctionals, in bijection.\n\nThis is what licenses replacing the former by the latter, and it was stated in\nprose before it was proved. The prose version only ever established the `←`\ndirection — that `⟪w, ·⟫` is linear — which on its own would permit the\nreplacement to have NARROWED the class of admissible traces. `→` is what rules\nthat out. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.weight_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.weight_unique","kind":"theorem","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/Common.lean#L167-L175","doc":"**Riesz, uniqueness direction**: the representing weight is unique. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.exists_weight_of_isLinearMap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.exists_weight_of_isLinearMap","kind":"theorem","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/Common.lean#L147-L165","doc":"**Riesz, surjective direction**: every `ℝ`-linear functional on `HeckeElement n`\nIS `⟪w, ·⟫` for some `w`.\n\nThis is the direction that carries the weight of the claim below, and it is the\none that is easy to assert and skip. `HeckeElement n` is a finite-dimensional\nreal inner-product space, so a linear map out of it is automatically continuous\n(`LinearMap.toContinuousLinearMap`) and `InnerProductSpace.toDual` is an\nisometric equivalence onto the dual. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.isLinearMap_frobeniusInner","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.isLinearMap_frobeniusInner","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/Common.lean#L138-L145","doc":"Every `frobeniusInner w` is an `ℝ`-linear functional. (The easy direction.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.markovTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.markovTrace","kind":"def","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/Common.lean#L110-L136","doc":"**Markov trace** on `H_n(q_0)`, as the linear functional with Riesz weight\n`markovTraceWeight n`.\n\nThe full categorical definition (Jones-Markov coefficients `y_λ`,\npartition-sum decomposition) lives in the rendered manuscript and the Python\ncompute layer; what is formalised here is that the trace is a linear\nfunctional, which is the only property the downstream SDP-uniqueness\narguments use.\n\n**Cyclicity is a separate matter** and remains an axiom\n(`MarkovTrace.MarkovTrace_cyclic`): it constrains this functional against\n`heckeMul`, which is itself `opaque`, so it is not expressible from the\nlinear-algebra layer alone.\n\n🛑 **This does NOT pin the trace to a non-zero function.** Taking\n`markovTraceWeight n = 0` satisfies this definition and every axiom stated\nabout `markovTrace` in `QOU.HeckeAlgebra.MarkovTrace`, since each of those\nreads `0 = 0` under it. That was already true of the previous `opaque`\npresentation and is unchanged here — but it is worth stating where a reader\nwill see it, because a sharper version of the same degeneracy was a live\ndefect: bean `qou-ck1f` found `MarkovTrace_markov_axiom` binding its Markov\nparameter with `∀ (z : ℝ)`, which PROVED `tr_M ≡ 0`. Removing that binder\nremoved the proof of degeneracy; it did not add anything excluding it.\nNothing in this layer forces `tr_M ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.markovTraceWeight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.markovTraceWeight","kind":"opaque","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/Common.lean#L90-L108","doc":"**Riesz weight of the Markov trace.**\n\n`HeckeElement n` is a finite-dimensional real inner-product space, so by\nRiesz representation EVERY `ℝ`-linear functional on it is `⟪w, ·⟫` for a\nunique `w`.  The Markov trace is such a functional, so nothing is lost by\ncarrying it as its weight vector rather than as an opaque function: the two\npresentations have exactly the same content.\n\nWhat IS gained is that linearity stops being assumed.  See\n`markovTrace_linear` below, which was an `axiom` until 2026-08-26.\n\nThe weight itself stays `opaque` because its VALUE is genuinely not\nformalised here — categorically it is the Jones-Markov combination\n`Σ_λ y_λ χ^λ` (`QOU.HeckeAlgebra.MarkovTrace.markovTraceOnWedderburn`\ncarries that form against a Wedderburn decomposition).  An `opaque`\ndatum asserts nothing; an opaque function plus an asserted property\nasserts something unprovable.  This is the difference. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.frobeniusInner_symm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.frobeniusInner_symm","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/Common.lean#L84-L88","doc":"The Frobenius inner product is bilinear-symmetric: `⟨x, y⟩ = ⟨y, x⟩`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.frobeniusInner_self_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.frobeniusInner_self_pos","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/Common.lean#L76-L82","doc":"The Frobenius inner product is positive on non-zero elements:\n`frobeniusInner x x > 0` for `x ≠ 0`.  Inherited from\nMathlib's `EuclideanSpace` inner-product structure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.frobeniusInner","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.frobeniusInner","kind":"def","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/Common.lean#L70-L74","doc":"**Frobenius inner product** on `H_n(q_0)`.  Standard inner\nproduct on the underlying Euclidean space, exposed under the\nQOU naming convention.  Symmetric, bilinear, positive-definite. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.HeckeElement","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.HeckeElement","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/Common.lean#L55-L68","doc":"**Abstract Hecke-algebra element** at `n` strands and parameter\n`q_0`.  Represented as a vector in `EuclideanSpace ℝ` of\ndimension `heckeDim n`, sufficient for the convex-analysis\narguments used downstream (Frobenius inner product, strict\nconvexity).  The full algebraic structure (multiplication,\nHecke relations, generators σ_i) is *not* exposed here; this\nmodule captures only the linear-algebra layer needed for the\nSDP arguments.\n\nConcrete categorical structure (Wedderburn decomposition,\nMarkov trace, generator action) is in scope for future work\nonce the Lean port of the Hoefsmit / Wenzl machinery lands. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.heckeDim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.heckeDim","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/Common.lean#L50-L53","doc":"**Hecke-algebra dimension** at `n` strands.  For type `A_{n-1}`,\n`dim_ℂ H_n(q) = n!`.  We use this dimension count whether `q`\nis a formal parameter or the QOU substrate value `q_0`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}